  "levelType": "practical",
  "statementHtml": "<p>Given the root of a binary tree. Return all the <strong>root-to-leaf paths</strong> in the binary tree.</p><p><br></p><p>A leaf node of a binary tree is the node which does not have a left and right child.</p>",
  "examples": [
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> root = [1, 2, 3, null, 5, null, 4]</p><p><strong>Output :</strong> [ [1, 2, 5] , [1, 3, 4] ]</p><p><strong>Explanation :</strong> There are only two paths from root to leaf.</p><p>From root 1 to 5 , 1 -> 2 -> 5.</p><p>From root 1 to 4 , 1 -> 3 -> 4.</p><p><img src=\"https://static.takeuforward.org/content/ProblemSetter-hHfCfcd8\"></p>",
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</p><p><strong>Output :</strong> [ [1, 2, 4] , [1, 2, 5] , [1, 3] ]</p><p><strong>Explanation :</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://static.takeuforward.org/content/ProblemSetter-w9T0EbU5\"></p>",
    "<p><strong>Input :</strong> root = [1, 2, 3, 4, null, 5, 6, null, 7]</p><p><img src=\"https://static.takeuforward.org/content/ProblemSetter-JU7Hm_WW\"></p>"
  ],
